## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/curvature.html
- Summary (EN): Computes the curvature of an input layer, useful for edge detection and for separating convex and concave regions. Similar in purpose to the Derivative COP.
- Résumé (FR) : Calcule la courbure d'une hauteur ou d'une normale pour détecter les bords et séparer zones convexes et concaves.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: a mono height-field layer, or an RGB normal vector field derived from a height field"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature / Space: layer type accepted and space used to measure curvature", "Method: Finite Difference (derivative-based, stable on smooth inputs) or Angle Deficit (polygon-vertex based, more robust on complex variations)", "Curvature Type: Gaussian, Mean, Principal (max) or Principal (min)", "Output Type: full curvature, convex regions only, or concave regions only", "Normal Type (pre-process): must match the Height to Normal node setting when the input is a normal field", "Read Pixels outside Image (pre-process): uses pixels beyond the edge at boundaries", "Kernel Size (pre-process): neighbourhood scale; larger gives smoother results", "Scale, Normalize, Minimum, Maximum (post-process): adjust, keep in 0 to 1, or clamp output"]

- Caveats: ["Normal Type must match Height to Normal or the input is misread.", "With a constant border type, turn off Read Pixels outside Image to get correct edge values.", "Minor pixel-to-pixel variation can give unexpectedly high values; Normalize may be needed for display."]

